Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-14-2000||11:36 AM||||i have a stock wheelbase 86 under my 308 Replica. But ive heard that there is enough slack to use the original with a stretch chassis. If not, shouldnt be too hard to make a longer threaded link where the original one is under left rear. Or even use a length of stainless stranded cable, with small U-clamps. <P>'quote' if it dont work - improvise !||||reg||1
Z||000004||86se/lambo||12-17-2000||03:13 AM||||i have a stretched fiero and what they do is reposition the e- brake handle towards the rear of the car using a a simple remounting bracket... this makes the cable longer. IFG in chino,ca offers this with their stretch kits. <A HREF="http://www.ifgonline.com" TARGET=_blank>www.ifgonline.com</A> ||||reg||1
